WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.630
We knew they were going to try everything
to try to get Donald Trump reelected and the

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.910
next step is sabotaging the post office.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:10.820
And this is super important to know about.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:16.340
So, yes, Donald Trump floated yesterday the
idea of delaying the presidential election.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.340
Unlikely to happen.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.590
He doesn't actually have the power to do it.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.090
He can mess up the post office pretty badly.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.240
And that's what he's trying next.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.730
So to set this up, Corona virus hits.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.710
But we know we have an election coming up
in November.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.710
OK.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.710
Simple solution.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:30.710
You vote by mail.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.240
And when we say vote by mail, we don't mean
some new system.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.960
We just mean expanding absentee ballot access
to anybody that wants an absentee ballot.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.310
Whether or not corona virus is under control
in November.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.310
We don't know.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.850
It's increasingly looking like it's going
to be out of control.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.200
But we expand absentee ballot access to everybody.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.239
We've got a solution for a safe election.

00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:52.360
Trump is against it.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.300
Trump is against it because he says there
will be fraud.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:00.720
Trump doesn't understand that vote by mail
is the same in this case as just absentee.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.770
We're not talking about a different system.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:06.159
He's either confused or he's lying or he's
distorting or whatever.

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:07.159
We don't know.

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:11.810
Well, governors mostly, fortunately, take
matters into their own hands and they expand

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.320
absentee ballots.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.950
They in some states say everybody can get
one.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.960
In others, they say you still have to have
a valid reason for requesting an absentee

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:21.960
ballot.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.140
But fear of catching Corona virus counts as
a valid reason.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.850
Some states are doing other types of expansions.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.500
But for the most part, governors do the right
things.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.090
So what is Trump's next move?

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:37.810
Well, he's trying to neuter and kneecap the
post office.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:41.310
Donald Trump has appointed Lewis Dejoy to
be postmaster general.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:46.770
Dejoy just happens to be a huge Trump donor
who wants to see Donald Trump reelected.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:52.400
And Dejoy has announced that he's going to
eliminate overtime for hundreds of thousands

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.579
of postal workers.

00:01:54.579 --> 00:02:00.610
Overtime widely expected to be needed as we
have a record number of people opting to vote

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:05.930
absentee rather than in-person, which could
delay mail services and, of course, prevent

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:07.890
the delivery of the ballots.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:13.609
In other words, Trump, through his postmaster
general, is trying to cause the very problems

00:02:13.609 --> 00:02:16.909
that he cited as the reason why we shouldn't
have vote by mail.

00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:21.480
Lewis Dejoy is also considering closing a
bunch of post offices across the country,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:26.000
and Dejoy is using kind of coded language
to try to hide his intentions, saying things

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.920
like, well, listen, we haven't done any kind
of reform in the post office for a long time.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.079
We're going to take a fresh look at the operations
of the Postal Service.

00:02:34.079 --> 00:02:35.120
This is all code.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.989
Now, we know that because of Corona virus
and because we know that absentee ballot access

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:47.449
has been expanded in a bunch of states around
the country, there will be way more absentee

00:02:47.449 --> 00:02:53.340
ballots this year than arguably in any prior
year.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.800
And we are just a few weeks from the start
of that, remember, four and a half weeks from

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.800
now.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.469
Some states start voting absentee.

00:03:01.469 --> 00:03:03.239
So what do they want to do?

00:03:03.239 --> 00:03:04.559
Cut the post office?

00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:07.040
This is completely obvious.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.760
Three months before an election, Trump puts
in a big donor to run the post office.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.889
And immediately, Trump's donor says, whoa,
whoa, whoa, stop the clock.

00:03:16.889 --> 00:03:18.859
Let's reduce mail service.

00:03:18.859 --> 00:03:21.900
What people are e-mailing me saying, how is
this legal?

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.689
That's a great question.

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:28.439
This is extremely authoritarian, something
we're now used to with Donald Trump.

00:03:28.439 --> 00:03:34.870
This is another example of regulatory capture
and this is another example of the right wanting

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.479
to suppress turnout.

00:03:36.479 --> 00:03:40.900
If you can't stop people from going to the
polls as easily because lots of people are

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:45.839
going to be voting by mail, prevent their
ballots from being delivered by hurting the

00:03:45.839 --> 00:03:46.839
post office.

00:03:46.839 --> 00:03:49.129
This is the strategy and it should be mentioned.

00:03:49.129 --> 00:03:56.199
You know, sometimes I point out Democrats
and Republicans are both part of maintaining

00:03:56.199 --> 00:04:01.900
this status quo, where they're both mostly
onboard with expanding the military budget

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.999
or whatever.

00:04:02.999 --> 00:04:06.709
This is not a both sides issue for is it 20
years?

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:07.799
Is it longer?

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:13.900
The right has had the strategy of trying to
hold down turnout in certain areas to try

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.569
to win elections.

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:16.989
The left doesn't do this.

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:21.289
The left doesn't consider as a top strategy
for winning elections.

00:04:21.289 --> 00:04:24.740
Let's figure out how to prevent people from
voting or how to prevent people's votes from

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:25.740
counting.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:31.069
So first of all, number one, we have to so
overwhelm the vote that these strategies won't

00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:32.069
work.

00:04:32.069 --> 00:04:36.629
I've been saying that for a year or longer,
and I hope that now everybody understands

00:04:36.629 --> 00:04:38.460
why it's true.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.990
Secondly, there is a maybe possible backfire
effect here.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:47.700
So right now, red states have been way more
hit by corona virus than blue states for now.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:52.870
This could mean that red states are doing
more online shopping because it's safer to

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.330
go shopping in blue states than red states.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:59.539
And so hurting the Postal Service might actually
anger more.

00:04:59.539 --> 00:05:01.000
Publican's than Democrats.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.090
Now, whether they'll link it to Trump's postmaster.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:06.590
And hold Trump accountable is another story.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:13.000
Remember that when Obamacare passed and Republican
governors opted not to do the Medicaid expansion.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.990
A lot of those red state voters blamed Obama.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:20.990
Even though Obama gave the governors the tools,
it was the governors who opted not to do it.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:24.870
They may not actually hold the right people
accountable, but they are doing it.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.479
They're doing it right now.

00:05:26.479 --> 00:05:31.430
This is not a dress rehearsal and that is
almost going to be the everybody must vote.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.110
And this is not a dress rehearsal or very
quickly becoming the phrases of the next three

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:35.629
months

